rd one tile from T8,T8,T3,T3? Actually we have T3,T3,T8,T8 before peng. Peng uses one T3 from table and our two T3, so our hand becomes T8,T8 plus new meld. We must discard one tile, so we discard one T8, remaining hand = T8 alone. So not a pair.  \n\nSo we\u2019d need to draw T8 to make a pair to win. Winning hand would be 4 melds + pair.  \n\nPoints:  \n- All Simples (2)  \n- Single wait (1)  \n- Self-drawn (1) if self-drawn  \n- Chicken hand? (8) but Chicken hand requires no other fans except Last Tile etc \u2014 actually Chicken hand is 8 points if no other fans, but All Simples already gives 2, so can\u2019t be Chicken.  \nSo total = 4 (if self-drawn) or 3 (if won on discard).  \n\nThat's less than 8, so **cannot win legally**.  \n\nThus **Peng is useless** \u2014 we should pass and try to change hand to a valid 8-point hand later.  \n\n**Reason:** Peng T3 leads to a hand that cannot reach 8 points given current melds, making winning impossible under MCR rules. Better to pass and keep flexibility to aim for higher-value patterns.  \n\n**Answer:** Pass"}
